FIXME Decide whether that will stay the recommended installation procedure, and copy over here.

You can also install the firmware without serial cable, but have a spare UART cable at your side for any issues you might encounter!

Make sure to have one original firmware at hand, maybe the current one or a newer version so you can write both partitions with that one in case of a failure.
Write them twice so you have the original on both.

Download/build latest sysupgrade image, ideally something after commit <code>70498cb3865e3ada4f1b47c55ead266c40fd4c3e</code> (snapshot image it's a bit old at the time of writing this because of build bot failure, I think, so maybe it's better to build yourself a recent one)

extract the kernel and root images using: <code>binwalk -e openwrt-qualcommax-ipq807x-qnap_301w-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin</code>

With booted QuRouter OS hold WPS button until second beep to enable ssh, login with:
<code>
ssh admin@192.168.100.1 -p 22200
sudo fw_printenv -n current_entry
</code>
if it's printing 1, you are good to go, if not do:

<code>
sudo fw_setenv current_entry 1
sudo reboot
</code>
verify again if the output is 1:

<code>
sudo fw_printenv -n current_entry
</code>
Copy the kernel and the root image to the device

<code>
scp -P 22200 kernel admin@192.168.100.1:/tmp/
scp -P 22200 root admin@192.168.100.1:/tmp/
</code>
Flash firmware and set boot partition to "0":

<code>
sudo dd if=/tmp/kernel of=/dev/mmcblk0p1
sudo dd if=/tmp/root of=/dev/mmcblk0p4
sudo fw_setenv current_entry 0
sudo fw_setenv boot_0 good
sudo reboot
</code>

It should boot to OpenWrt, now install firmware for 10G phys.
Check if partition mtd10 and backup somewhere outside the device for any chances:

<code>
cat /proc/mtd|grep "0:ethphyfw"
dd if=/dev/mtd10 of=/tmp/ethphyfw.backup
</code>
if you are using the recommended minimum image version you should have 2 10G firmware partitions: 
<code>
mtd10: 00080000 00010000 "0:ethphyfw1"
mtd11: 00080000 00010000 "0:ethphyfw2"
</code>
You can get the 10G firmware from the original firmware or use the github files from https://github.com/0x5826/Marvel-AQR-FW, <code>AQR-G4_v5.4.C-AQR_CIG_WF-1945_0x0_ID44778_VER1630.cld</code> and <code>AQR-G4_v5.4.C-AQR_CIG_WF-1945_0x8_ID44776_VER1630.cld</code>

Write the images to fw1 and fw2 region, assuming you downloaded them in the /tmp location (you could use wget and download them from github)

Pay extra attention **<color #ed1c24>NOT</color>** to make any typo and erase mtd1 because you will lose your partition Information and the device will not boot anymore!

Get the mtd values
<code>
mtd_ethphyfw1=$(grep "ethphyfw1" /proc/mtd | awk -F: '{print "/dev/" $1}')
mtd_ethphyfw2=$(grep "ethphyfw2" /proc/mtd | awk -F: '{print "/dev/" $1}')
</code>

Verify the correct values
<code>
echo $mtd_ethphyfw1
#should output /dev/mtd10
echo $mtd_ethphyfw2
#should output /dev/mtd11
</code>
Write firmware to flash
<code>
mtd erase "$mtd_ethphyfw1"
mtd -n write /tmp/AQR-G4_v5.4.C-AQR_CIG_WF-1945_0x0_ID44778_VER1630.cld "$mtd_ethphyfw1"

mtd erase "$mtd_ethphyfw2"
mtd -n write /tmp/AQR-G4_v5.4.C-AQR_CIG_WF-1945_0x8_ID44776_VER1630.cld "$mtd_ethphyfw2"
</code>
reboot and you are good to go:
<code>
 dmesg | grep NVMEM
[    1.830094] Aquantia AQR113C 90000.mdio-1:00: loading firmware version 'v5.4.C CIG WF-1945_0x0 060120 02:47:48' from 'NVMEM'
[   13.369392] Aquantia AQR113C 90000.mdio-1:08: loading firmware version 'v5.4.C CIG WF-1945_0x8 060120 02:47:48' from 'NVMEM'
</code>

If your settings aren't saved after reboot, install sysupgrade in OpenWrt.
Copy sysupgrade file using SCP (WinSCP in Windows):
<code>
scp openwrt-qualcommax-ipq807x-qnap_301w-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin root@192.168.1.1:/tmp/
</code>

Then do a sysupgrade:
<code>
sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-qualcommax-ipq807x-qnap_301w-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
</code>

